          "depth": 1,
          "epoch": 1,
          "hypothesis": "For sufficiently large grids, work-sharing fixed column chunks can parallelize each row's prefix recurrence while retaining rolling-row memory; compact reset-or-add chunk summaries preserve the left-to-right dependency. Small grids avoid OpenMP scheduling overhead.",
