          "delegation_parent": "R/C",
          "depth": 1,
          "epoch": 1,
          "hypothesis": "A tiled diagonal wavefront exposes independent tile work while preserving the north/west path dependencies. For larger grids, static OpenMP work sharing across 32x32 tiles should amortize scheduling over useful work; rolling tile-edge buffers and sparse per-row obstacles avoid an N×N allocation. Small grids stay on a serial rolling-row path.",
          "id": "c320cf54ab8b4572",
          "ordinal": 2,
          "parent_id": null,
          "role": "C",
          "source_commits": [],
          "sources": [],
          "transformations": {
            "files": [
              "src/solution.cpp"
            ],
            "retained": [
              "Store blocked columns by row instead of allocating a dense N×N blocked-cell bitmap; use a serial rolling-row recurrence for n < 512.",
              "For larger grids, process 32×32 tiles in diagonal wavefront order, work-share each wave with OpenMP schedule(static), and retain only the preceding wave's bottom and right tile edges."
            ]
          },
          "tree_id": "e1:C",
