      "mother_plan:synthesis": {
        "model_calls": 1,
        "phase": "synthesis",
        "plan": {
          "A": "Research obstacle representation and free-run traversal. Compare sorted, deduplicated per-row lists against packed-bit scanning, preferably with contiguous storage to reduce allocations. Produce strip-local free-run access suitable for C's pipeline without constructing a quadratic blocked grid. Preserve duplicate-coordinate semantics and all boundary cases; measure preprocessing plus computation.",
          "B": "Research ARM64 SIMD free-run kernels starting from deb870c2dc304003. Compare eight-cell unrolling with larger independent prefix-scan groups and scalar handling of short runs. Maintain modular reduction after each scan stage, safe unaligned access, and exact tails. Make the kernel usable within column strips with an incoming carry and returned boundary value. Use only the existing compiler and supported instructions.",
          "C": "Refine the fastest measured pipeline, 8087bf3fada8499d. Compare up to four workers, strip widths, and row-batch sizes around 16 to balance startup latency, synchronization, and locality. Investigate bounded spinning versus yielding without changing runtime permissions. Preserve release/acquire publication of immutable edge values and correctness when the actual OpenMP team is smaller than requested. Retain a measured serial fallback.",
          "G": "Use 8087bf3fada8499d at 0.01237 s as the incumbent. Integrate B's free-run SIMD kernel into C's strip pipeline, then independently evaluate A's obstacle representation. Measure each combination end to end; do not assume additive gains. Keep the fastest validated complete program, including the unchanged incumbent if integrations regress. Verify duplicates, blocked endpoints, n=1, strip and SIMD tails, and reduced team sizes through existing permitted validation. Do not alter tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, or permissions.",
          "analysis": "The source implements Problem D, not the other problems in the supplied document. Its quadratic traversal, blocked-grid allocation, row copying, and per-cell remainder dominate the baseline's 0.07885 s. Measured candidates favor the batched strip pipeline at 0.01237 s over barrier-based parallel scans at 0.01776 s; the improved SIMD kernel reaches 0.01940 s, while scalar sparse representations reach 0.02276–0.02416 s. These measurements motivate combining parallel dependency scheduling with SIMD free runs, while evaluating representation costs separately. All paths must compute the original recurrence modulo 1000000007 for every valid input; four ARM64 cores and no GPU constrain the research."
        },
