            "B": "Research row-level parallelism for the stencil update using the existing compiler/toolchain. Use race-free writes and a per-iteration logical-OR reduction for the convergence flag; ensure every worker finishes before the next iteration or buffer swap. Keep output serialized and ordered. Measure parallel overhead and use a general workload-based cutoff if beneficial; do not tune to particular test cases or change the target or compiler.",
            "C": "Research an exact active-region optimization based on the source's fixed initialization: track a conservative bounding box containing all potentially nonzero cells and expand it by one cell per iteration, clipped to the grid. Cells outside it have zero neighbors, so their update and error are both zero; skip them only while that invariant is maintained. Include fixed boundary values in the initial bounds, preserve the exact convergence decision and final update, and fall back to a full sweep when the active region is no longer profitable. Validate across all supplied cases and measure the result.",
