          "depth": 1,
          "epoch": 1,
          "hypothesis": "A persistent OpenMP team amortizes startup across all simulation iterations, while static worksharing distributes equal-cost target and integration loops; a generic body-count threshold keeps small inputs serial. This should improve full-program time on the four-core target without changing each target's ascending source-body accumulation order.",
          "id": "a4febcec1ab0420b",
          "ordinal": 1,
          "parent_id": null,
