    "mother_plans": {
      "mother_plan:preparation": {
        "model_calls": 1,
        "phase": "preparation",
        "plan": {
          "A": "Develop a conservative copy/allocation-reduction candidate without changing search order. Pass immutable graphs, matrices and vectors by const reference, targeting Prim_ST, find_min_key, is_cycle, coresConjunto, buscaSequencial and the graph arguments throughout recursion. Do not turn mutable hist into a shared reference without explicit backtracking. Replace the scan-to-last partition operation with equivalent back/pop_back handling; move containers only when ownership genuinely ends. Reserve or reuse scratch storage with complete resets. Keep spanning-edge, inclusion/exclusion and partition order unchanged. Deliver an independently measured candidate and identify changes that B and C can safely reuse.",
          "B": "Optimize tree-path enumeration. Build tree adjacency once per spanning tree, appending both endpoints in the original spanning-edge order so buscaAresta's neighbor order is reproduced exactly. Use one backtracked path, visited state and incremental color-frequency counts instead of path copies, linear membership searches and leaf-time color recounting. Support arbitrary valid color ranges through dynamic storage or label compression. Save caminho only on a strict improvement. Preserve ascending starting vertices, ordered recursive exploration, leaf-only evaluation and the first K-color leaf: reaching K colors internally must not emit a shorter path. Optionally investigate sound pruning only when a branch cannot reach K and cannot strictly improve contCor; do not reinterpret pruned internal nodes as leaves. Measure this separately from A.",
          "C": "Optimize deterministic spanning-tree construction. Prove and exploit the redundant cycle machinery: retained mat_cycle entries cannot leave root 0 because parent[u] > 0 excludes them, while initial root trials contain only one arc. Remove that machinery only with a complete invariant argument. Since every usable edge has weight 1, investigate an ordered discovered-vertex frontier instead of repeated copied key scans. Preserve lowest-vertex selection, ascending neighbor scans, first-discovery parents and the original inclusion predicates, including sentinel behavior. Investigate immutable ascending adjacency plus exclusion masks/stamps rather than cloning the dense graph for every Prim_ST call. Preserve spanning-edge output order, partition insertion/LIFO order and failure/return semantics; a conventional constrained-MST replacement is not automatically equivalent. Prioritize serial savings over threading at this runtime.",
          "G": "Integrate only programs produced by A/B/C, using the supplied selected base commit. Within the unchanged budget, compare individual candidates and promising incremental combinations with the fixed correctness and timing machinery. Keep the fastest supported correct candidate, including an individual tree's program or the baseline if integration loses. Do not assume gains add. Audit restored scratch state, adjacency ordering, Prim tie-breaking, partition order, leaf selection, strict incumbent updates and exact output formatting. Require general semantic justification, not merely success on the four observed cases. Treat small timing differences cautiously relative to the baseline's approximately 0.16 ms observed spread. Do not alter tests, oracle, compiler, target, permissions or budgets, and do not specialize to measured inputs or expected answers.",
          "analysis": "Focus exclusively on Maximum Tropical Path in src/tropical.cpp. The only measurement is a correct baseline on four cases: mean 5.680 ms, with samples spanning 5.576–5.737 ms. There is no hotspot profile or evidence of an optimization win yet. Source inspection suggests avoidable graph/matrix/container copying, repeated tree-edge scans, leaf-time color recounting and redundant cycle checks. These are hypotheses to measure, not established runtime shares. On four ARM64 CPU cores without a GPU, this short baseline favors low-overhead serial improvements before parallel overhead. Reference compatibility requires preserving the selected ordered path and formatting, not merely producing some path with the same color count."
        },
