    "mother_plans": {
      "mother_plan:preparation": {
        "model_calls": 1,
        "phase": "preparation",
        "plan": {
          "A": "Research bounded-memory exact top-k selection in the KNN kernel. Compare a minimally changed sorted list with immediate rejection against the full list's worst distance, and a max-heap whose root is the worst (distance, encounter index) pair. Heapify the initial candidates, replace only when a new candidate is better, and preserve earlier points at equal distances. Target O(P log k) worst-case selection with O(k) auxiliary storage; coordinates still need storage because the query arrives last. Investigate exact runtime paths for k=1 and k=P, without assuming either occurs in the measurements. Preserve reference behavior for NaNs and unfilled slots through explicit handling or a reference fallback. Keep parsing unchanged initially to isolate the kernel improvement. Deliver the best validated candidate and its automatic timing evidence to G.",
          "B": "Research materialized selection as an alternative to A, not an additional selection stage. Compute records containing the original float squared distance, global encounter index and label; partition by the first two fields and count the first k records without sorting them. Use quickselect with an explicit poor-partition fallback to avoid pathological quadratic behavior. Compare its expected linear work against record-allocation and memory-traffic costs. If concurrency is supported by the unchanged build, investigate up to four disjoint chunks: each retains its exact local top min(k, chunk size), then select the global top k from their union. Global encounter indices must survive every partition and merge. Retain a serial implementation for workloads where threading or the candidate union costs more. Use source-faithful fallback for unordered distances. Report complete-program timings, correctness results and memory trade-offs, not just distance-loop throughput.",
          "C": "Research input conversion, storage and voting independently of the selection algorithm. Replace repeated scanf overhead experimentally with buffered fread parsing and strtof, or an equivalently proven float conversion. Preserve the source's n_groups= grammar, whitespace rules, single-character label handling, signs, exponents and other valid float forms; do not assume fixed decimal precision or convert through double without an equivalence argument. Handle tokens across buffer boundaries and do not require seekable stdin. The query follows all points, so retain sufficient coordinates and label metadata; compare compact storage against the existing per-group allocations without assuming copying pays off. Replace label qsort with a byte-frequency histogram, aggregating repeated labels and resolving equal frequencies in the order induced by compare_for_sort on the target's plain char type. Preserve any unfilled sentinel labels. Initially retain the original selector to isolate frontend and voting gains, and provide G a separable candidate with measured evidence.",
          "G": "Integrate only correctness-valid programs produced by A/B/C. First compare their standalone end-to-end results; then prioritize C's frontend/voting with the best selector, testing the alternative selector combination if the fixed budget permits. A and B are competing selection kernels, not cumulative optimizations. Reconcile storage interfaces and retain the exact float, encounter-order, label-order and fallback contracts. Consider runtime dispatch only from general workload properties such as P and k, supported by measured crossover evidence—not test identities, coordinate patterns or expected labels. Measure each integrated binary with the unchanged automatic harness: improvements are not additive, and allocation, cache traffic or thread overhead can make integration slower than either input. Retain the fastest validated measured program, including a standalone candidate or baseline when appropriate. Record source lineage, correctness status and timing samples. Do not alter tests, oracle, compiler, flags, budgets, target or permissions.",
          "analysis": "The supplied sources concern only Problem A, KNN; A/B/C below are research roles, not contest problems. Let P be the total number of points. The baseline scans and shifts a length-k neighbor list for O(Pk) work, then sorts labels; scanf conversion is another plausible cost, but no phase profile or input-size distribution is supplied. The only measured program passed four correctness cases and averaged 2.01547 seconds, with samples from 2.01133 to 2.02049 seconds. No proposed gain is established yet. The target is four ARM64 CPU cores with no GPU. Correctness requires the reference's float squared-distance evaluation and rounding, not approximate arithmetic. For non-NaN distances, selection is equivalent to ordering by distance and original group-major encounter index: equal distances favor earlier points. Frequency ties favor the smallest label under the target's plain-char comparator, not group order. The statement supplies no useful coordinate or k bounds: optimized paths must preserve source-defined corner cases, including NaNs and remaining char(-1) slots when k exceeds P, rather than invent new restrictions. Four passing cases alone do not establish equivalence for all valid inputs."
        },
        "request_sha256": "2c468f231c09dcbaa717443717528fc0af3f7a5f0640dbd074cf6541b1de0697",
        "response": {
          "data": {
            "A": "Research bounded-memory exact top-k selection in the KNN kernel. Compare a minimally changed sorted list with immediate rejection against the full list's worst distance, and a max-heap whose root is the worst (distance, encounter index) pair. Heapify the initial candidates, replace only when a new candidate is better, and preserve earlier points at equal distances. Target O(P log k) worst-case selection with O(k) auxiliary storage; coordinates still need storage because the query arrives last. Investigate exact runtime paths for k=1 and k=P, without assuming either occurs in the measurements. Preserve reference behavior for NaNs and unfilled slots through explicit handling or a reference fallback. Keep parsing unchanged initially to isolate the kernel improvement. Deliver the best validated candidate and its automatic timing evidence to G.",
            "B": "Research materialized selection as an alternative to A, not an additional selection stage. Compute records containing the original float squared distance, global encounter index and label; partition by the first two fields and count the first k records without sorting them. Use quickselect with an explicit poor-partition fallback to avoid pathological quadratic behavior. Compare its expected linear work against record-allocation and memory-traffic costs. If concurrency is supported by the unchanged build, investigate up to four disjoint chunks: each retains its exact local top min(k, chunk size), then select the global top k from their union. Global encounter indices must survive every partition and merge. Retain a serial implementation for workloads where threading or the candidate union costs more. Use source-faithful fallback for unordered distances. Report complete-program timings, correctness results and memory trade-offs, not just distance-loop throughput.",
            "C": "Research input conversion, storage and voting independently of the selection algorithm. Replace repeated scanf overhead experimentally with buffered fread parsing and strtof, or an equivalently proven float conversion. Preserve the source's n_groups= grammar, whitespace rules, single-character label handling, signs, exponents and other valid float forms; do not assume fixed decimal precision or convert through double without an equivalence argument. Handle tokens across buffer boundaries and do not require seekable stdin. The query follows all points, so retain sufficient coordinates and label metadata; compare compact storage against the existing per-group allocations without assuming copying pays off. Replace label qsort with a byte-frequency histogram, aggregating repeated labels and resolving equal frequencies in the order induced by compare_for_sort on the target's plain char type. Preserve any unfilled sentinel labels. Initially retain the original selector to isolate frontend and voting gains, and provide G a separable candidate with measured evidence.",
            "G": "Integrate only correctness-valid programs produced by A/B/C. First compare their standalone end-to-end results; then prioritize C's frontend/voting with the best selector, testing the alternative selector combination if the fixed budget permits. A and B are competing selection kernels, not cumulative optimizations. Reconcile storage interfaces and retain the exact float, encounter-order, label-order and fallback contracts. Consider runtime dispatch only from general workload properties such as P and k, supported by measured crossover evidence—not test identities, coordinate patterns or expected labels. Measure each integrated binary with the unchanged automatic harness: improvements are not additive, and allocation, cache traffic or thread overhead can make integration slower than either input. Retain the fastest validated measured program, including a standalone candidate or baseline when appropriate. Record source lineage, correctness status and timing samples. Do not alter tests, oracle, compiler, flags, budgets, target or permissions.",
            "analysis": "The supplied sources concern only Problem A, KNN; A/B/C below are research roles, not contest problems. Let P be the total number of points. The baseline scans and shifts a length-k neighbor list for O(Pk) work, then sorts labels; scanf conversion is another plausible cost, but no phase profile or input-size distribution is supplied. The only measured program passed four correctness cases and averaged 2.01547 seconds, with samples from 2.01133 to 2.02049 seconds. No proposed gain is established yet. The target is four ARM64 CPU cores with no GPU. Correctness requires the reference's float squared-distance evaluation and rounding, not approximate arithmetic. For non-NaN distances, selection is equivalent to ordering by distance and original group-major encounter index: equal distances favor earlier points. Frequency ties favor the smallest label under the target's plain-char comparator, not group order. The statement supplies no useful coordinate or k bounds: optimized paths must preserve source-defined corner cases, including NaNs and remaining char(-1) slots when k exceeds P, rather than invent new restrictions. Four passing cases alone do not establish equivalence for all valid inputs."
          },
