    "mother_plans": {
      "mother_plan:preparation": {
        "model_calls": 1,
        "phase": "preparation",
        "plan": {
          "A": "Research an isolated serial selection variant. The current inner insertion is O(points*k); preserve its observable ordering by ranking ordinary candidates as (float distance, global encounter order), where equal distances retain the earlier group/point. Compare a small-k sorted buffer, max-heap, and deterministic selection; for k near the total point count, evaluate selecting the N-k farthest points and subtracting their labels from total counts. Replace the final label qsort only if the exact char-comparator tie behavior is retained. Keep an original-semantics fallback for exceptional float/order cases; do not use fast-math, double arithmetic, or approximate distances.",
          "B": "Research an isolated input/layout throughput variant. Parsing and allocation may materially contribute to the 2.06 s end-to-end baseline, so investigate a buffered, grammar-preserving textual reader with correctly rounded float conversion and all valid whitespace/punctuation accepted by the source. Flatten points into contiguous coordinates plus labels while reading, then evaluate distances in a cache/SIMD-friendly pass without changing the float expression or reassociating it. Measure full-program benefit, not just parsing or a kernel; storage is necessary because the query arrives after the training points.",
          "C": "Research an isolated exact ARM64 four-core variant. Parallelize after parsing with deterministic contiguous shards: each worker retains its local best k (or local farthest N-k for the complement path), then a deterministic merge chooses the global set. This is exact when the secondary key is the global encounter index. Explore a serial/parallel threshold so OpenMP setup and merge costs do not hurt smaller inputs, avoid shared heap contention and nondeterministic reductions, and retain exact voting/output behavior. Account for the serial input stage when evaluating end-to-end speedup.",
          "G": "Act as sole integrator of complete variants from A/B/C. Do not assume their gains compose: first validate and time each full candidate on the existing evaluation path, then remeasure every combination retained. Use the current correct baseline (mean 2.0556327359 s across 2.0248458, 2.0112657, 2.1307867 on 4-core ARM64) as the comparison point. Reject any candidate that changes strict-distance cutoff ties, equal-frequency label choice, textual-input acceptance, or the one-character stdout contract. Audit boundary ties, k extremes, repeated distances, and unusual labels; preserve a safe fallback where an optimization cannot reproduce baseline floating behavior. Keep compiler, target, oracle, budgets, and execution constraints unchanged.",
          "analysis": "The only measurement is a correct baseline with four correctness cases and no measured alternatives. Its dominant algorithmic liability is insertion into a length-k sorted array for every point, while scanf-style parsing may also limit achievable parallel speedup. Correctness must match the supplied sequential program, not merely an abstract KNN definition: points are encountered in group/point order; insertion uses strict '<', so cutoff ties are stable; labels are then sorted and a mode tie follows that comparator's order. A, B, and C therefore explore orthogonal full-program variants—selection, ingestion/layout, and parallel selection—while G makes evidence-based integration."
        },
        "request_sha256": "492ffb6f17ecacaf2120fc65deb0ffdab8e7d7cbb6da904636fb73a607b16e7a",
        "response": {
          "data": {
            "A": "Research an isolated serial selection variant. The current inner insertion is O(points*k); preserve its observable ordering by ranking ordinary candidates as (float distance, global encounter order), where equal distances retain the earlier group/point. Compare a small-k sorted buffer, max-heap, and deterministic selection; for k near the total point count, evaluate selecting the N-k farthest points and subtracting their labels from total counts. Replace the final label qsort only if the exact char-comparator tie behavior is retained. Keep an original-semantics fallback for exceptional float/order cases; do not use fast-math, double arithmetic, or approximate distances.",
            "B": "Research an isolated input/layout throughput variant. Parsing and allocation may materially contribute to the 2.06 s end-to-end baseline, so investigate a buffered, grammar-preserving textual reader with correctly rounded float conversion and all valid whitespace/punctuation accepted by the source. Flatten points into contiguous coordinates plus labels while reading, then evaluate distances in a cache/SIMD-friendly pass without changing the float expression or reassociating it. Measure full-program benefit, not just parsing or a kernel; storage is necessary because the query arrives after the training points.",
            "C": "Research an isolated exact ARM64 four-core variant. Parallelize after parsing with deterministic contiguous shards: each worker retains its local best k (or local farthest N-k for the complement path), then a deterministic merge chooses the global set. This is exact when the secondary key is the global encounter index. Explore a serial/parallel threshold so OpenMP setup and merge costs do not hurt smaller inputs, avoid shared heap contention and nondeterministic reductions, and retain exact voting/output behavior. Account for the serial input stage when evaluating end-to-end speedup.",
            "G": "Act as sole integrator of complete variants from A/B/C. Do not assume their gains compose: first validate and time each full candidate on the existing evaluation path, then remeasure every combination retained. Use the current correct baseline (mean 2.0556327359 s across 2.0248458, 2.0112657, 2.1307867 on 4-core ARM64) as the comparison point. Reject any candidate that changes strict-distance cutoff ties, equal-frequency label choice, textual-input acceptance, or the one-character stdout contract. Audit boundary ties, k extremes, repeated distances, and unusual labels; preserve a safe fallback where an optimization cannot reproduce baseline floating behavior. Keep compiler, target, oracle, budgets, and execution constraints unchanged.",
            "analysis": "The only measurement is a correct baseline with four correctness cases and no measured alternatives. Its dominant algorithmic liability is insertion into a length-k sorted array for every point, while scanf-style parsing may also limit achievable parallel speedup. Correctness must match the supplied sequential program, not merely an abstract KNN definition: points are encountered in group/point order; insertion uses strict '<', so cutoff ties are stable; labels are then sorted and a mode tie follows that comparator's order. A, B, and C therefore explore orthogonal full-program variants—selection, ingestion/layout, and parallel selection—while G makes evidence-based integration."
