      "mother_plan:synthesis": {
        "model_calls": 1,
        "phase": "synthesis",
        "plan": {
          "A": "Own state storage and allocation. Keep fb723bd4c27a4ed2 as an optional compact-layout variant, preserving offsetof-based sizing and proper alignment. Investigate generating serial successors into reusable aligned scratch, probing exact membership before allocating permanent states. Scratch must never enter the arena free list, visited table, or frontier; accepted states must retain the original parent and coordinates. Measure the extra accepted-state copy against avoided duplicate allocation/recycling. Do not retain 374fee23e28c4a9d's sorting change by default: it measured worse. Preserve the exact player position and sorted box list, not merely push-equivalent states.",
          "B": "Use f1034fed2c134d0c as the SIMD incumbent. Its actual diff already includes e178223f1540418e's occupancy lookup, so these are not independent improvements. Preserve bounded NEON loads, first-match behavior, scalar tails/fallbacks, and unsigned modulo-2^32 hash equivalence. Evaluate restoring the full-hash equality check before lookup's memcmp as a separate, small variant: different full hashes cannot represent equal coordinate arrays. Measure rather than assume that the extra hash load or SIMD setup helps small box counts. Keep all decisions based on general runtime sizes.",
          "C": "Own deterministic parallel expansion. Develop 3e278194bfca4c39 while retaining its small-frontier serial path and bounded scratch allocation. Workers may prepare candidates and probe a read-only visited table; allocation, resizing, duplicate rechecks, parent selection, and first-success selection must remain serial in the original parent and right/left/up/down order. Preserve prepended-frontier ordering and barriers separating probes from mutations. Establish whether the parallel path actually contributes under this run's measurements. Keep 36aead14bf9147a6's parallel rehash independent: it has no demonstrated gain, and composing it with expansion can introduce nested-team overhead. Use only the existing build and four-core target.",
          "G": "Start integration from f1034fed2c134d0c, retaining baseline and standalone candidates as controls. First evaluate the best B program combined with C's deterministic wide-frontier expansion. Consider admissible A storage/allocation or B lookup descendants individually afterward; retain a combined program only on its own correctness and end-to-end measurement. Do not merge the occupancy-only B patch twice, automatically include the slower sorting/rehash variants, or infer additive gains. Reconcile shared successor and lookup changes carefully, especially scratch ownership and serial duplicate rechecks. Preserve exact solution text, traversal, push capitalization, and termination behavior. If combinations do not improve measured performance, retain the best standalone program rather than the largest patch.",
          "analysis": "The ARM64 four-core baseline is 4.982 ms. Best B is 4.892 ms, C expansion 4.918 ms, and occupancy-only B 4.926 ms. Layout and parallel rehash are slightly slower at 5.003 and 5.008 ms; insertion sorting is worst at 5.218 ms. Baseline samples span 4.816–5.116 ms, exceeding the apparent winning margins, so rankings are provisional. Four correctness cases are evidence, not a general proof. This is full-state, minimum-player-movement Sokoban search. The reference's right/left/up/down generation and prepended level lists make exact path selection sensitive; do not silently replace that traversal with a conventional queue based on the statement's tie wording."
        },
