    "mother_plans": {
      "mother_plan:preparation": {
        "model_calls": 1,
        "phase": "preparation",
        "plan": {
          "A": "Research CPU parallelism while retaining the original scalar interaction loop. Assign independent target bodies i to at most four workers using threading already supported by the frozen build. Preserve ascending j accumulation and the original arithmetic. Use persistent workers across all ten steps where practical, with a barrier after velocity updates before any position changes, and another before the next force phase. Compare one, two and four workers, including startup and synchronization costs. Do not parallelize the j reduction.",
          "B": "Research exact ARM64 SIMD across independent target bodies, not across the j reduction. Process several i targets in separate lanes while traversing j in its original order. Preserve float displacement, distance and accumulation semantics; the reference reciprocal is double-precision division by sqrt(double(sqrd_dist)), subsequently rounded to float. Explore paired double-precision SIMD sqrt/divide operations with float lanes for the surrounding work. Match the frozen reference's contraction behavior. Do not substitute sqrtf, reciprocal-square-root estimates or reassociated reductions. Retain an exact scalar tail and fallback wherever equivalence is unproven; include any packing costs in measurements.",
          "C": "Research exact unordered-pair distance reuse as an independent alternative. Initialize O(n) force accumulators, visit lower endpoint i increasingly, include its self interaction at the correct point, then visit j>i increasingly. Earlier rows have already supplied target i's contributions from sources below i, so this traversal can preserve every target's original source order. Share only a provably identical distance/reciprocal calculation; compute reverse displacements and directed accumulation expressions independently rather than negating an already-rounded force. Establish equivalence under the frozen floating-point behavior, including overflow and signed zero. Use the original directed kernel whenever nonfinite coordinates or other unproven conditions invalidate that argument. Start serially and measure whether saved sqrt/divide work outweighs additional accumulator traffic.",
          "G": "Integrate only validated candidates and measure each resulting whole program independently. Prioritize combining A's target parallelism with B's target-lane SIMD, preserving both timestep barriers and scalar numerical semantics. Evaluate C separately: its shared accumulators make naive parallelization of its outer loop incorrect. Combine it with threading only through an explicitly ordering-preserving, race-free design, such as disjoint block-pair wavefronts. Preserve input/output framing and validate every integration with the unchanged oracle. Compare measured mean runtime against each constituent and the baseline; retain the fastest correct measured program, including the baseline if necessary. Do not assume gains are additive.",
          "analysis": "The active task is Problem C, nbody; A/B/C are research-role names. This run supplies only a correct baseline: four correctness cases and a 0.65893-second mean from three closely grouped timings. There is no measured candidate speedup or hotspot profile. The source suggests ten quadratic interaction passes, particularly sqrt/divide work, as the main opportunity on four ARM64 CPU cores without a GPU. Preserve all ten synchronous steps, DT, softening, and correctness for every valid input. Read the leading body-count integer followed by six floats per body; output only the body records. Treat binary numerical equivalence conservatively because no tolerance is documented here. Keep compiler, build settings, tests, oracle, budgets and target unchanged; all proposed gains remain hypotheses until measured."
        },
        "request_sha256": "72005f87f9e1fe90186dc8941bd41b7cfd04be879aa2167b95406db280808c45",
        "response": {
          "data": {
            "A": "Research CPU parallelism while retaining the original scalar interaction loop. Assign independent target bodies i to at most four workers using threading already supported by the frozen build. Preserve ascending j accumulation and the original arithmetic. Use persistent workers across all ten steps where practical, with a barrier after velocity updates before any position changes, and another before the next force phase. Compare one, two and four workers, including startup and synchronization costs. Do not parallelize the j reduction.",
            "B": "Research exact ARM64 SIMD across independent target bodies, not across the j reduction. Process several i targets in separate lanes while traversing j in its original order. Preserve float displacement, distance and accumulation semantics; the reference reciprocal is double-precision division by sqrt(double(sqrd_dist)), subsequently rounded to float. Explore paired double-precision SIMD sqrt/divide operations with float lanes for the surrounding work. Match the frozen reference's contraction behavior. Do not substitute sqrtf, reciprocal-square-root estimates or reassociated reductions. Retain an exact scalar tail and fallback wherever equivalence is unproven; include any packing costs in measurements.",
            "C": "Research exact unordered-pair distance reuse as an independent alternative. Initialize O(n) force accumulators, visit lower endpoint i increasingly, include its self interaction at the correct point, then visit j>i increasingly. Earlier rows have already supplied target i's contributions from sources below i, so this traversal can preserve every target's original source order. Share only a provably identical distance/reciprocal calculation; compute reverse displacements and directed accumulation expressions independently rather than negating an already-rounded force. Establish equivalence under the frozen floating-point behavior, including overflow and signed zero. Use the original directed kernel whenever nonfinite coordinates or other unproven conditions invalidate that argument. Start serially and measure whether saved sqrt/divide work outweighs additional accumulator traffic.",
