          "depth": 1,
          "epoch": 1,
          "hypothesis": "Removing the repeated cycle-detection BFS and its matrix is a low-overhead CPU experiment: each Prim relaxation connects a selected vertex to an unselected one, so even the include/exclude filters cannot make that attachment close a cycle. This avoids adding OpenMP launch overhead to the small measured workload.",
