      {
        "id": "0c5069bf3ecc495f",
        "role": "B",
        "state": "completed",
        "mission": {
          "base_commit": "5f440ebece77b116d291bb21248cf308f6a9202c",
          "delegation_parent": "R/B",
          "depth": 2,
          "epoch": 1,
          "hypothesis": "For sufficiently large arrays, OpenMP tasks on the disjoint recursive quicksort ranges can use the available CPU cores while retaining the serial partition loop whose boundary index has a loop-carried dependency. A task-size cutoff should limit scheduling overhead; serializing pivot RNG draws avoids races without changing the sorted result.",
