            ],
            "retained": [
              "For arrays over 32 elements, use stable signed-order 8-bit LSD radix passes with a sequential scratch buffer; retain quicksort when scratch allocation fails, and use insertion sort for smaller arrays.",
              "Build all byte histograms in one input sweep, then scatter through stable contiguous passes.",
              "Use a static-scheduled OpenMP SIMD bitwise-OR reduction for the sortedness check, activating the parallel team only for large inputs.",
              "Use Hoare partitioning with a selected pivot moved to the midpoint in the allocation-failure fallback; recurse on the smaller partition, iterate over the larger one, and insertion-sort ranges of at most 24 elements."
            ]
          },
