            "G": "Use C’s OpenMP candidate (0.0455 s; correct on 4 cases) as the incumbent against the 0.0667 s baseline. Integrate A’s buffer swap as a separate measured combination, ensuring both buffers have identical boundaries and the final completed sweep is the output. Evaluate B’s reduction variant separately; do not merge all changes by default. Run correctness and timing on each integrated candidate, and retain only combinations that are correct and actually faster. The contiguous-storage candidate measured 0.0615 s, so do not assume it helps either.",
            "analysis": "The measured best is C’s OpenMP worksharing candidate at 0.04546 s versus the 0.06667 s baseline, on a 4-core ARM64 target. Standalone buffer swapping was about 0.0584–0.0585 s; contiguous storage was 0.06148 s; the SIMD/row-flag version was 0.06745 s. These results support using C as the incumbent, while treating further optimizations and combinations as experiments. Preserve Jacobi iteration, convergence and output semantics for every valid input."
