    "mother_plans": {
      "mother_plan:preparation": {
        "model_calls": 1,
        "phase": "preparation",
        "plan": {
          "A": "Research replacing the O(P·k) sorted-array insertion in src/knn.c with a bounded max-heap, targeting O(P log k). Preserve the baseline’s stable handling of equal distances by ranking candidates on (squared distance, original encounter index); benchmark across input sizes and k values, and verify output correctness rather than assuming a speedup.",
          "B": "Research CPU parallelization suited to the measured ARM64 target (4 cores, no GPU): partition the encountered points into contiguous ranges, compute private top-k candidate sets, then deterministically merge them using the same distance-and-encounter-order ranking as the baseline. Measure thread overhead and end-to-end performance; use only mechanisms compatible with the existing build setup.",
          "C": "Research an introselect-based alternative for regimes where k is large relative to P: compute candidate records, select the first k by (squared distance, encounter index), and tally their labels without sorting all P candidates. Assess its O(P) extra-memory cost and worst-case behavior; compare correctness and timings against the baseline and the other approaches.",
          "G": "Integrate only candidate programs produced by A/B/C. First measure each candidate independently, then measure the integrated program as a whole—do not assume gains add. Preserve exact classification behavior, including distance ties and vote ties, and select or dispatch among approaches only when correctness and end-to-end measurements support it. Do not alter tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, or permissions.",
          "analysis": "The current source is Problem A’s KNN classifier. Its baseline scans P points and may inspect/shift up to k entries per point, then sorts k labels; squared Euclidean distances avoid square roots. The sole automatic measurement is a correct baseline (4 cases), mean 2.0356777108584843 seconds over three runs [2.0604070760309696, 2.0158473001793027, 2.03077875636518], score 0.5. No candidate or integration measurements are provided, so these are research hypotheses, not demonstrated improvements. All approaches must remain general and preserve baseline tie behavior."
        },
