          "hypothesis": "Combining median-of-three three-way partitions, insertion sort for tiny ranges, and a depth-limited heapsort fallback should keep serial sorting efficient and robust. For large arrays, disjoint OpenMP tasks above a cutoff can exploit the four-core target without changing generated values or output.",
