      "mother_plan:synthesis": {
        "model_calls": 1,
        "phase": "synthesis",
        "plan": {
          "A": "Build on the measured winner: contiguous row-major byte adjacency storage with cached row pointers (0.00687 s versus the 0.00841 s baseline). Explore verifier/access improvements on that layout, measuring each change independently. The packed-bit candidate was slower (0.00742 s), so do not assume denser storage is faster. Preserve correctness and output behavior.",
          "B": "Research low-cost, exact graph-invariant filters, starting with degree-multiset rejection after the existing identity fast path. The measured degree-filter candidate was 0.00781 s versus 0.00841 s baseline, but slower than A’s winner; test it on the winning layout and isolate filter costs. Preserve all valid mappings and their required output behavior.",
          "C": "Investigate semantics-preserving ways to reduce permutation-verification work, prioritizing a sequential approach and exact pruning that preserves output ordering. Treat parallel batching as unproven: the measured batched candidates took 0.00951 s and 0.01308 s, both slower than baseline. Only pursue parallelism further if measurements show a workload threshold where its overhead pays off.",
          "G": "Use A’s contiguous-byte candidate (0.00687 s) as the current measured integration starting point, not as a guaranteed final winner. Integrate tree-produced changes one at a time, then measure combinations because gains may not add. Validate correctness and output ordering on the full allowed inputs; retain only measured, correct improvements. Do not alter tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, permissions, or source outside the assigned integration work.",
          "analysis": "The baseline mean is 0.00841 s. The strongest observed result is A’s contiguous row-major byte matrix with cached row pointers at 0.00687 s. Other measured candidates—packed bits (0.00742 s), SIMD (0.00767 s), and degree filtering (0.00781 s)—beat baseline but not that result. Both OpenMP batching candidates regressed. Guidance therefore centers on the measured layout, carefully measured exact filters, and avoiding unproven parallel overhead. The source’s identity shortcut and permutation emission behavior should remain intact unless correctness validation establishes otherwise."
        },
