    "mother_plans": {
      "mother_plan:preparation": {
        "model_calls": 1,
        "phase": "preparation",
        "plan": {
          "A": "Research a low-risk serial algorithmic improvement to the current Problem B solution. The baseline scans serpentine S×S windows and updates each one in O(S), giving O(SN²) work. Explore separable rolling sums that find the maximum in O(N²), using 64-bit accumulators and preserving correctness for every valid N, S, and matrix. Compare with the baseline on the unchanged correctness and timing harness; report the algorithm, memory use, and measured results.",
          "B": "Independently investigate implementation-level improvements for Problem B: input parsing, flat versus vector-of-vectors storage, cache behavior, and safe accumulator/output choices. Consider alternatives such as prefix sums only if their memory costs are measured against the N<8000 limit. Keep the full computation general, preserve exact maximum-sum behavior, and report correctness and timing evidence rather than assuming an I/O or layout change helps.",
          "C": "Explore a parallel approach to Problem B that can use the target's 4 ARM64 CPU cores, while accounting for memory bandwidth, temporary storage, synchronization, and thread startup overhead. Compare it against the best serial O(N²) candidate, including cases where parallel overhead may outweigh gains. Preserve correctness for all valid inputs and report complete measured timings and memory costs.",
          "G": "Integrate only candidate programs produced by A, B, and C. Check each candidate's correctness and resource use, then benchmark promising candidates and the integrated program with the unchanged harness. Do not presume gains combine additively: measure the final integration against its components and baseline, and retain the best verified general solution. Do not alter tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, permissions, or unrelated source.",
