            "C": "Research a parallel comparison-sort candidate for the ARM64 four-core target: sort bounded chunks of indices, then merge them with the same `strcmp` ordering, with a serial fallback for small inputs. Cap parallelism at the available cores and measure one- versus multi-thread performance; avoid races and unbounded scratch storage.",
            "G": "Integrate only candidates produced by A, B, and C, and preserve the best verified full-program result. Run correctness and timing checks on each candidate and each proposed combination: gains may not be additive, and integration can be slower than its inputs. Keep comparison/order semantics and behavior correct for every valid input; do not tailor to test data.",
            "analysis": "The task is bucketsort. In the supplied baseline source, each bucket uses insertion sort over indices with `strcmp`, giving a likely quadratic cost within large buckets; fixed per-bucket storage also merits care if bucket sizes are uneven. The only automatic measurement is a correct baseline run across 4 cases: mean 0.42005 s (samples 0.41999, 0.41831, 0.42185) and score 0.5. There are no measured optimized candidates, so these are opportunities to investigate, not established speedups. The target is ARM64 with 4 CPU cores."
