            "B": "Refine the strongest measured candidate: direct recurrence evaluation with a circular buffer for small distance d=H−N. Measure a general crossover across N and d, and choose dispatch based on robust evidence rather than a particular input. Preserve chronological window and reversed-coefficient alignment, verify modular bounds for block accumulation, and check boundary cases. The measured 4-way unroll was slower than the original short-distance branch, so retain it only if new measurements justify it.",
            "C": "Independently investigate Bostan–Mori for the recurrence’s generating function as an alternative general large-H path. Derive the numerator from the given initial terms and denominator coefficients, and validate index parity and coefficient extraction carefully, including N=1. Compare it with A’s approach and the existing matrix path; avoid duplicating A’s implementation. The measured OpenMP/transposed-matrix variants were slower than baseline, so do not assume parallelism or transposition helps on this four-core ARM64 target.",
