            "C": "Research ordered parallel generation on the four ARM64 CPU cores, using only threading facilities supported by the unchanged build. Partition the sorted multiset into unique lexicographic prefix subtrees; each task enumerates its remaining suffix in order. Assign tasks lexicographic sequence numbers and use a single ordered writer with bounded buffering and backpressure. Ensure later tasks cannot exhaust buffering resources needed by the earliest unfinished task. Explore coarse task sizes and limited adaptive prefix splitting rather than one task per permutation. Avoid duplicate prefixes, cross-subtree permutations, and overflow-prone factorial ranking. Measure against buffered sequential generation, retaining a general sequential fallback when startup, synchronization, or insufficient independent work outweighs parallelism.",
